{"content":{"author":"/root/tail_capture_design_audit","blocks":[{"text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/tail_capture_design_audit\nPayload:\nDecision memo: final-session tail capture\n\nRoot cause\n\n- `Stop` and `SessionEnd` currently run the same immediate capture path in [claude-code.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/src/adapters/claude-code.ts) and [qwen-code.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/src/adapters/qwen-code.ts).\n- The host waits for that hook, then appends closing transcript records. Therefore a blocking sleep inside the hook cannot solve it: it delays the very write it is waiting for.\n- The next-session sweep recovers tracked sessions, but never the final session if no later session runs. It must remain as a fallback for crashes and exits that never emit `SessionEnd`.\n\nCurrent upstream constraints\n\n- Claude supports `async: true`, but explicitly kills unfinished async hooks when a headless `claude -p` session tears down and says to start a fully detached process when work must outlive the session: [Claude hooks reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#run-hooks-in-the-background).\n- Qwen’s async hooks are scoped to the Qwen process and reclaimed on POSIX exit unless the event explicitly promises fire-and-forget completion. `SessionEnd` makes no such promise: [Qwen hooks documentation](https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code/blob/main/docs/users/features/hooks.md).\n- Consequently, setting `async: true` is not the fix for either adapter. The cledger process must create its own detached child.\n\nRecommendation\n\nKeep the existing synchronous capture. On `SessionEnd` only, have it launch a detached cledger finalizer with ignored stdio and `unref()`:\n\n1. Wait 500 ms after the parent hook returns.\n2. Capture the named transcript.\n3. Poll its size every 250 ms.\n4. Recapture whenever it changes.\n5. Finish after 1 second of quiescence, with a 10-second hard cap.\n6. Preserve the repository context/anchor observed by the `SessionEnd` hook so a commit made immediately after exit cannot mis-anchor the tail.\n7. Coalesce finalizers per source/session. Duplicate execution would still be data-safe because event IDs deduplicate, cursor writes are atomic, and Annals serializes note writes, but coalescing avoids needless processes.\n8. Retain the current sweep as crash/no-`SessionEnd` recovery.\n\nA blocking poll and host-managed async hook are both unsuitable. A fixed one-shot delay is viable but weaker than bounded stability polling.\n\nRollout recommendation\n\nShip Claude first, then Qwen in a separate PR after its own live headless test.\n\n- Claude has direct live evidence: a cursor stopped at line 40 of 50, with the useful final snapshot at line 49.\n- Qwen has the same architectural exposure, but current 0.21.9 has substantially evolved hook lifecycle behavior. A separate PR keeps any source-specific correction isolated.\n- The shared finalizer machinery can be introduced in the Claude PR and reused by Qwen.\n\nJudgment needed\n\n- Failure visibility: I recommend keeping a small per-session local finalizer job/error record under `.git/conversation-ledger/`, deleting it on success, retrying it on the next hook, and warning then if it previously failed. The simpler alternative is silent failure plus the existing sweep.\n- Rollout: Claude-first as recommended, or enable Claude and Qwen together.\n- The proposed 500 ms / 1-second quiet / 10-second cap is conservative and imposes no exit latency because the worker is detached.\n\nCompatibility hazards\n\n- Windows needs `detached: true`, ignored stdio, `unref()`, and `windowsHide: true`; environments using Windows Job Objects may still kill descendants, so Windows requires separate validation.\n- SIGKILL, OS shutdown, immediate worktree deletion, or uninstalling/moving cledger during the delay can defeat the worker. The retained sweep/job retry covers everything except a permanently abandoned last session.\n- Detached stderr cannot safely remain attached to a departed TUI or headless pipe; diagnostics need local state rather than inherited output.\n- Multiple `SessionEnd` reasons include `/clear` and interactive `/resume`, not only process exit. Finalizing those transcripts is appropriate.\n- Qwen’s latest docs now describe command-hook timeout values as seconds, while retaining millisecond compatibility for values of 1000 or greater. The existing `120000` remains 120 seconds, but the code comment saying Qwen always uses milliseconds is now stale.\n\nMinimal live test, no TUI inspection\n\nAfter building/linking the candidate and running `cledger install claude-code`:\n\n```sh\nprobe=$(mktemp -d)\ngit -C \"$probe\" init -q\ngit -C \"$probe\" config user.name TailProbe\ngit -C \"$probe\" config user.email tail@example.invalid\ntouch \"$probe/seed\"\ngit -C \"$probe\" add seed\ngit -C \"$probe\" commit -qm init\n\nmarker=$(mktemp)\n(cd \"$probe\" && claude -p 'Reply with exactly: tail-probe')\nsleep 12\n\ntranscript=$(find \"$HOME/.claude/projects\" -type f -name '*.jsonl' -newer \"$marker\" -print | head -n 1)\nsession=${transcript##*/}\nsession=${session%.jsonl}\ncursor=\"$probe/.git/conversation-ledger/cursors/$session.json\"\n\nnode -e '\nconst fs=require(\"fs\");\nconst [cursor, transcript]=process.argv.slice(1);\nconst saved=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(cursor,\"utf8\")).size;\nconst actual=fs.statSync(transcript).size;\nconsole.log({saved, actual, complete:saved===actual});\nprocess.exit(saved===actual ? 0 : 1);\n' \"$cursor\" \"$transcript\"\n\n(cd \"$probe\" && cledger capture claude-code --transcript \"$transcript\")\n```\n\nExpected:\n\n- `complete: true`\n- Manual recapture reports `+0 events`\n\nRepeat with `qwen -p 'Reply with exactly: tail-probe'` and locate the new transcript under `~/.qwen/projects`. This headless case specifically proves that the finalizer survives host teardown. No files were changed during this audit.","type":"text"}],"recipient":"/root","role":"agent_message"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"a6821c75dddf42529c15a1402d89fb01aaae50a9","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-64952bd5b74814c3460db48077740dba68b077773621f1ee9ff4fc19a1f8ba1b","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"/root/tail_capture_design_audit","type":"agent"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai","session_id":"01a0d132-3af5-7f63-9ce8-f92787b93442","source":"codex","source_version":"0.156.1"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-25T01:32:32.064Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw":{"data":{"ordinal":1850,"payload":{"author":"/root/tail_capture_design_audit","content":[{"text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/tail_capture_design_audit\nPayload:\nDecision memo: final-session tail capture\n\nRoot cause\n\n- `Stop` and `SessionEnd` currently run the same immediate capture path in [claude-code.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/src/adapters/claude-code.ts) and [qwen-code.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/src/adapters/qwen-code.ts).\n- The host waits for that hook, then appends closing transcript records. Therefore a blocking sleep inside the hook cannot solve it: it delays the very write it is waiting for.\n- The next-session sweep recovers tracked sessions, but never the final session if no later session runs. It must remain as a fallback for crashes and exits that never emit `SessionEnd`.\n\nCurrent upstream constraints\n\n- Claude supports `async: true`, but explicitly kills unfinished async hooks when a headless `claude -p` session tears down and says to start a fully detached process when work must outlive the session: [Claude hooks reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#run-hooks-in-the-background).\n- Qwen’s async hooks are scoped to the Qwen process and reclaimed on POSIX exit unless the even